  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  data:
    name: 'Fenestra Cochlea/ Round window '
    detail: 'The Fenestra Cochleae, or Round Window, is a small circular opening
      on the lower posterior part of the medial wall of the middle ear.

      It
      leads into the scala tympani of the cochlea and is closed by a secondary tympanic
      membrane that separates the air of the middle ear from the perilymph of the
      inner ear.'
