  data:
    name: 'Chorda Tympani nerve '
    detail: 'The chorda tympani is a branch of the facial nerve (cranial nerve VII)
      that passes through the middle ear cavity between the mucosal and fibrous layers
      of the tympanic membrane.

      It carries taste fibers and secretomotor fibers.'
