  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  data:
    name: Incus
    detail: 'The incus (anvil) is the second ossicle in the middle ear chain, linking
      the malleus to the stapes.

      It lies mainly in the epitympanum (attic)
      and acts as a lever transmitting sound vibrations from the malleus handle to
      the stapes footplate at the oval window.'
