  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  data:
    name: 'Canal for Tensor Tympani muscle '
    detail: 'The canal for the tensor tympani muscle is a bony tunnel located in
      the anterior (carotid) wall of the middle ear cavity, above the opening of
      the Eustachian tube.

      It contains the tensor tympani muscle, which helps
      regulate tension on the tympanic membrane.'
