  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  data:
    name: 'Internal Carotid Artery '
    detail: "The Internal Carotid Artery (ICA) runs in close relation to the anterior
      (carotid) wall of the middle ear cavity.\nIt is separated from the tympanic
      cavity by a thin bony plate\u2014sometimes only a few millimeters thick (about
      3 mm) or even congenitally dehiscent, making the artery visible or pulsatile
      within the middle ear."
